From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:17:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Keep the GPU on and quiet in
 system sleep

The G16 firmware keeps running across suspend-to-idle: keep its GFX
domain on through system sleep, and hold its idle ring-service kicks in
the mailbox instead of waking the system about twice a second.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit 4b2b3de62d6b944991c38939a475dbf6b842eabc)
[dylan: J604 form of the J713 change: same two flags on the J604's own
 agx_mbox and &ps_gfx nodes in t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi (flags only, no
 values). Without them the J604 G16 driver, which has no system-sleep
 callbacks, has its GFX domain and the TVM gate above it powered off by
 genpd in the noirq phase under the running firmware, as on the J713.]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi
index 60ee2d8a55..c1b60a4644 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi
@@ -91,6 +91,8 @@
 		/* ASCWrap v6 contains the same mailbox aperture used by ASC v4. */
 		compatible = "apple,t8132-asc-mailbox", "apple,asc-mailbox-v4";
 		reg = <0x3 0x02608000 0x0 0x4000>; /* DTV-GPU-8 */
+		/* Idle ring-service kicks need not wake the system. */
+		apple,hold-rx-in-sleep;
 		interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
 		interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 993 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>, /* DTV-GPU-9 */
 			     <AIC_IRQ 994 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
@@ -111,4 +113,6 @@
 &ps_gfx {
 	status = "okay";
 	power-domains = <&gfx_tvm>;
+	/* The G16 firmware stays live across suspend-to-idle. */
+	apple,sleep-retained;
 };
